    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0284" n="208" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg208"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.60d Finnish Vessels/162</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Finnish Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Järnefelt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-07-26">July 26, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to Your Excellency’s note
                    of April 12, regarding the claims growing out of the detention by the United
                    States of thirteen Finnish sailing vessels, I have the honor, having been
                    authorized by my Government, to inform you that the statements, arguments and
                    conclusions set forth in the memorandum handed to the Legal Adviser of the
                    Department of State, Mr. Hackworth, on January 30, and in the reply of the
                    claimants to the answer of the United <pb facs="0285" n="209" xml:id="pg209"/>
                    States of March 4, handed to the Legal Adviser of the Department of State on
                    April 4, are to be regarded as reflecting the views and position of the Finnish
                    Government.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eero Järnefelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
